% in 2026. IV has crept up but is not at an extreme.\n- **Skew:** It is flat, so there is no unusual premium on the downside or the upside.\n\n**What's missing:** I had no strike, expiry, premium, delta or underlying price. I couldn't compare IV with realised volatility or check whether the price embeds a fair expected move.\n\n**Risk behind the price:** Other nodes' findings suggest the fundamentals are less certain than the options market implies.\n- Utilities make up 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham Power is 35% of those and Norvane is 21%.\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering and scaled back procurement.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp to 165bp in Q3.\n- Data-centre grid connection growth is slowing to 9% in 2027.\n- Utility 2027 capex plans are still up (Pellham +18%, Norvane +12%).\n\nThat concentration in two customers may justify a slightly higher IV than the median.\n\n**Conclusion:** The pricing is neutral. Adding to LEAPS needs a view on the Pellham and Norvane funding risk, not an expectation of cheap options. Before sizing, check the specific contract's premium against your target move, and consider a spread to reduce vega cost.","ttft_ms":1888,"type":"result","duration_ms":25177,"uuid":"78ad0456-8a60-46d6-8a1b-116c76260ce0","ttft_stream_ms":998,"time_to_request_ms":111,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":15,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":15,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":13,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":61,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":197,"process_anon_m